===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*falwaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*pel-}}.

Cognate with Old Saxon {{m|osx|falu}}, Middle Dutch {{m|dum|valu}}, {{m|dum|vale}} (Dutch {{m|nl|vaal}}), Old High German {{m|goh|falo}} (German {{m|de|fahl}}), Old Norse {{m|non|fǫlr}}. The common Germanic is cognate with Latin {{m|la|pallidus}}, Ancient Greek {{m|grc|πελιτνός}} and Old Armenian {{m|xcl|ալիք||wave, gray hair}}.

